00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.740
So one of the most common excuses
I hear from people, uh, who profess

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:33.210
want to learn languages, uh, is that
they simply don't have the time.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.220
That's right up there with, you know,
you have a talent for, talking to

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.900
me, you have a talent for languages.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.519
I don't, I can't learn languages, which
normally refers back to their experience

00:00:44.519 --> 00:00:49.290
at school where in fact, they didn't learn
like most kids, at least in Canada, but

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.849
the other one is I don't have the time.

00:00:50.849 --> 00:00:52.500
People say that I don't have the time.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.880
So people seem to have time for
lots of activities, perfectly valid,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.220
like meeting with their friends
and watching TV or going hiking or

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.530
bicycling or whatever they like to do.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:08.630
But for whatever reason, they can't
find the time to learn languages.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.540
Typically, what that means is I have
other activities that I prefer to do.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.930
I have other activities that
are more valuable to me than

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:19.910
learning languages, which is fine.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:25.935
Not everybody has to learn languages,
but how then, because we have busy lives,

00:01:25.935 --> 00:01:31.065
our professional or working lives are
other activities are social activities,

00:01:31.245 --> 00:01:34.995
so how do you create time, find time,
make time for learning language?

00:01:35.765 --> 00:01:39.575
To me, the secret for me is listening.

00:01:40.205 --> 00:01:42.785
Listening is the easiest thing to do.

00:01:43.505 --> 00:01:45.245
I can listen first thing in the morning.

00:01:45.245 --> 00:01:46.355
I can listen in the car.

00:01:46.355 --> 00:01:48.155
I can listen wherever I am.

00:01:48.815 --> 00:01:51.055
And the listening is the trigger.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:58.200
And um, in many languages and I think
it goes back to Aristotle, uh, many

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.310
languages sort of say, you know, the
first step is the most important step.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.020
The beginning is the job...

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.910
well begun is the job half done.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:13.065
Uh, Chairman Mao said the 10,000
Long March began with, with one step.

00:02:13.245 --> 00:02:17.325
The main thing is to get started
and it's so easy to just listen.

00:02:17.625 --> 00:02:21.405
And then that triggers the rest of
it, but you have to know how to do it.

00:02:21.555 --> 00:02:25.455
So first of all, make
sure you equip yourself.

00:02:25.525 --> 00:02:25.975
Okay.

00:02:26.065 --> 00:02:30.355
So in my case, I listen
from a number of devices.

00:02:30.805 --> 00:02:33.175
I can listen on my iPad.

00:02:33.735 --> 00:02:37.665
So this is normally where I
work, you know, on LingQ, but

00:02:37.665 --> 00:02:39.795
I can put it on my stepper.

00:02:39.795 --> 00:02:42.675
Not, not everyone has a stepper
at home, obviously, but I can have

00:02:42.675 --> 00:02:46.395
this open in the background in
the morning when I do my exercise.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:52.830
Using this, um, program that
I'm on, which is on my iPhone.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:57.630
I have my iPad open and I'm
listening to my, whatever it is,

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.030
Persian, Arabic and so froth.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:04.020
So I use my iPad, but at the other
end of the spectrum, if I go running,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.780
jogging in the park, I take my, um, iPod.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.810
I should have brought this little
device I have that attaches to my

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:16.260
arm so that I just have my iPod here.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:17.489
It's light.

00:03:17.519 --> 00:03:18.359
This is why I use it.

00:03:18.359 --> 00:03:19.109
It's lighter.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:24.000
I could take my phone, which I'm
using to record this video, but of

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.350
course it's much bigger and heavier.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.670
So this is ideal for that.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:27.230
Okay.

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:29.820
And this, you know, I have
to load up ahead of time.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:33.690
So I have to make sure I use the
wifi at home to get whatever content

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.929
I want to listen to onto my iPod.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.240
So listening devices.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:44.670
Uh, also with both the, um, iPod
and, uh, well on all three of

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.590
them, I can subscribe to podcasts.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:54.690
Um, I can import, uh, audio and put
